From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 18:25:45 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] x86: decode the forms hardware rejects or accepts

Several encodings decoded differently from hardware:

- LEA, MOVHPS's store, MOVNTQ, and FXSAVE, FXRSTOR and XSAVE take a
  memory operand only; their register forms are undefined.
- BT, by register or by immediate, and CMP only read their operand
  and cannot be locked; LOCK BT and LOCK CMP are undefined.
- MOV to CS, or to a segment register past GS, is undefined before
  the source is read.
- SYSEXIT outside ring 0 raises #GP, not #UD.
- BSF and BSR ignore an F2 prefix.
